tasks/BACKLOG.md:252:🧩 **F-2426-1 — s2425’S DECLARED BOUNDARY MEASURED AND DISCHARGED: THE INDIRECT-REACH HOLE IS EMPTY TODAY, FORWARD-LIVE, AND DELIBERATELY NOT WIDENED (s2426, 2026-09-01; A NEGATIVE RESULT BANKED WITH ITS MECHANISM).** s2425 cured the marker census’s THIRD conjunct and closed its row with a declared boundary naming the FIRST: *“a guard reaching playwright INDIRECTLY — `npm run test:e2e -- --list` names no `playwright` literal … is a genuine hole and is the next place I would look.”* **I looked. It is EMPTY.** 📊 **RE-MEASURED over the same 174 `scripts/*.test.mjs`: `6` carry the list flag, and the ONLY one lacking the `playwright` literal is `worker-type-coverage.test.mjs` — the `tsc --listFiles` file s2425 had ALREADY classified and correctly excluded. ZERO live offenders; no collection guard reaches playwright indirectly today.** ⚠️ **EMPTY IS NOT IMPOSSIBLE, AND THAT IS THE HALF WORTH CARRYING (F-2214-1: record the MECHANISM, not the verdict, so the next fire inherits a reason): the idiom is ordinary house style here, so the boundary is FORWARD-LIVE rather than hypothetical — `12` of the 174 test files already spawn `npm`, and `7` `package.json` scripts wrap playwright (`test`, `test:preview`, `test:release`, `test:release-base`, `test:asset-diet`, `census`, `verify:visual`). A future collection guard written as `npm run test:preview -- --list` satisfies conjuncts 2 and 3 and is invisible to conjunct 1 — silently, in the one direction that file exists to make loud.** 🚫 **DELIBERATELY NOT WIDENED, on s2425’s OWN `fork` reasoning rather than on inertia, and MEASURED rather than assumed: the intersection of “spawns npm” and “carries the list flag” is exactly ONE file and it is SELF, already exempt by name — so widening buys NO detection today, while `npm` is common enough in this corpus to eventually meet the other two conjuncts and accuse an honest file: the noise that gets a guard excused into uselessness (F-1460-1).** ➡️ **THE NUMBER TO WATCH IS NAMED AT THE SITE so this cannot decay into prose: whether any npm-spawning test file ever gains the list flag. On the day that intersection exceeds SELF, re-measure and widen; until then a red would fire only on honest work.** ⚖️ **SEVERITY: NOT A DEFECT AND NOT A CURE — stated plainly so it is not over-read. Nothing was broken, no verdict moves, and the guard is green 9/9 before and after a COMMENT-ONLY edit. What changed is that a hole recorded as UNMEASURED is now measured, with its expressibility priced, so no future fire spends a budget re-deriving it.** 💡 **THE REUSABLE HALF: this streak has spent six fires learning to *enumerate the keys a selector uses*; the rung above it is that A DECLARED BOUNDARY IS AN UNCLAIMED MEASUREMENT (F-2219-1) — and the cheapest one on any board, because its author has already done the hard part of naming exactly where to look. **Take your predecessor’s declared limit before you take their recommended cure: the limit costs minutes and either retires an aim or hands you the next finding.** Here it retired one.** Evidence: `a66c712f4` (comment amendment, `scripts/collection-guards-subject-set-guard.test.mjs`). Guard green 9/9, 0.51 s, rooted in `test:ledger-guards`.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:515:🔬 **F-2320-1 — F-2318-2 REPRODUCED, DIAGNOSED TO ITS MECHANISM, AND RE-FRAMED: IT IS NOT ONE TEST'S RED, IT IS A FILE-WIDE TEARDOWN RACE WHOSE VICTIM ROTATES — AND MY OWN CURE FOR IT IS REFUTED, SO NOTHING LANDED (fire s2320 2026-08-26; discharges the s2319 handoff's item (C), which three fires had carried unowned).** ⚙️ **THE INHERITED FRAMING IS WRONG IN TWO WAYS AND BOTH MATTER.** (1) **THE COUNT: F-2318-2 records "three `THREE.GLTFLoader` texture-blob console errors". Measured: ONE.** The `+3` in the playwright diff counts ADDED DIFF LINES — `+ Array [`, the entry, `+ ]` — not array members; the reverse control is the `- 1` on the same header, which is the single line `- Array []`. **A diff header is not a census, and this one has been carried as an error count through three handoffs.** (2) **THE SUBJECT: it is not `run-suspend.spec.ts:194`'s red.** 📊 **MEASURED ACROSS NINE FULL RUNS, `--workers=1` throughout per §3.1, each arm's own validity asserted first (F-2215-1): PRISTINE main / mobile / `wave-boundary` ALONE → FAIL **2 of 2** · PRISTINE / desktop / same test alone → PASS · PRISTINE / desktop / FULL FILE → PASS 5/5 · **PRISTINE / mobile / FULL FILE → FAIL 1, and the casualty is `legacy no-controls` (line 297) while `wave-boundary` PASSES.** The error is emitted once per run and **whichever test happens to be navigating when a texture is in flight catches it.** So a fire that gates this file by running the named test alone, and a fire that runs the whole file, are looking at two different tests and one shared defect. 🔑 **THE MECHANISM, MEASURED NOT INFERRED, by a document-level probe on `index.html` that enriches the console error with the blob's own metadata (probe reverted in the same fire; tree verified pristine):** `REASON=FETCH-REJECT TypeError: Failed to fetch`, `visibility=hidden`, `ageMs=11–13`, `size=1994204`, `type=image/png`, `revoked=false`. **The document is UNLOADING.** `GLTFLoader` picks `ImageBitmapLoader` on chromium (`GLTFLoader.js:2600–2606`), which `fetch`es the blob URL; a `page.goto`/`reload` aborts every in-flight fetch, the promise rejects, and `GLTFLoader.js:3366`'s `.catch` logs `console.error` **unconditionally** — there is no callback a caller can supply to suppress it. ⚖️ **THEREFORE THE ERROR IS A TEARDOWN ARTEFACT AND NOT A PLAYER-VISIBLE FAULT: the texture is being fetched for a scene the browser is discarding.** Nothing is broken for the player; what is broken is a zero-console-error gate that is structurally unable to tell an abort from a decode failure. ✅ **THREE HYPOTHESES REFUTED BY MEASUREMENT, each of which would have been a real asset defect:** (a) **missing `mimeType`** — refuted, `type=image/png` at the failure, and a scan of **all 444 GLBs / 443 embedded images found ZERO lacking `mimeType`**; (b) **premature `revokeObjectURL`** — refuted, `revoked=false` at the moment of failure; (c) **image-decode memory cap** — refuted, the texture is **1024×1024** (≈4 MiB RGBA), two orders below the repo's largest embedded texture (`hero-3d.glb`, 4096×2048). 🎯 **THE ASSET IS IDENTIFIED EXACTLY: a 1024×1024 PNG of `1,994,204` bytes, embedded BYTE-IDENTICALLY in five dry-gulch landmark GLBs** — `ruined_mining_operation`, `bison_skeleton`, `cactus_thicket`, `abandoned_farmhouse`, `isolated_spring` (`assets/pilots/map-rebuild-spike/landmarks/dry-gulch/`). They load together when the spec swaps to `contract=e1-dry-gulch`, so five separate blob URLs carry one image and five fetches are in flight at once — which is why that navigation is the widest window, and why mobile loses it: `devices['Pixel 5']` runs at `deviceScaleFactor 2.75`, so the same work takes longer and is still pending at `goto`. ⛔ **MY CURE IS REFUTED AND DELIBERATELY NOT LANDED — THIS IS THE HALF WORTH INHERITING.** The obvious fix is to wait out the race on the game's own settle signal (`canvas.dataset.assetLoadingState === 'ready'`, the pattern `e2e/asset-diet.spec.ts:202` ("dieted output keeps two terrain census views and town within screenshot tolerance") already uses) before navigating away. **It appeared to work and the appearance was luck:** cure v1 took mobile `wave-boundary` alone from FAIL 2/2 to PASS and the mobile full file to **5/5 green** — and then the PRISTINE control returned the same 4-passed/1-failed shape at a different test, proving that 5/5 sits inside normal variance and was never evidence. **Cure v2, which also settles before the `legacy` test's navigation, STILL FAILED on mobile.** 🔑 **THE REASON IS STRUCTURAL AND KILLS THE APPROACH, NOT THE PARAMETERISATION: `assetLoadingState` is published only by `trackedGltfLoader` (`src/assets/AssetLoading.ts:13–35`), and most GLB call sites bypass it entirely with a bare `new GLTFLoader()`** — `pools.ts:1515`, `Game.ts:4757`, and the five boss systems among them. **So `ready` means "every loader I happen to track is done", never "no texture is in flight", and it can read `ready` while five untracked landmark fetches are pending.** A wait on that signal is a wait on a number that does not count the thing being waited for. ⚠️ **RECORDED BECAUSE A GREEN NEARLY SHIPPED ON IT: the one 5/5 run was produced by the fix, reported by the fix, and meant nothing — F-2215-1's rule generalises past controls to CURES. A cure validated only on the arm that was already deterministic has not been validated at all; take the reverse control on the PRISTINE tree before believing your own green.** 🔺 **OWNER'S FORK — this is a GATE-SEMANTICS decision, not a code fix, so no fire should take it unilaterally.** **(a) ACCEPT THE SIGNATURE (recommended as the immediate unblock):** filter exactly `THREE.GLTFLoader: Couldn't load texture blob:` from this spec's console-error bucket, with the mechanism above quoted at the filter. Cheap, reversible, restores a trustworthy gate — and costs real coverage: a genuinely corrupt GLB texture would then also pass unseen. **(b) MAKE THE SIGNAL HONEST (the real fix, ~8 call sites, needs a master):** route every `new GLTFLoader()` through `trackedGltfLoader` so `assetLoadingState` means what its name says, then (a)'s filter becomes unnecessary because the wait becomes sound. **(c) LEAVE IT:** a mobile gate that reds roughly one run in two, at a rotating test — which §3.1's own law calls worse than no test. **rec: (a) now, (b) when a lane is free.** ⓘ **NOTHING WAS LANDED THIS FIRE: `e2e/`, `src/` and `index.html` were all verified pristine at `git status --porcelain` after the last probe was reverted.** The deliverable is the diagnosis, the refutation, and the fork.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:661:✅ **BARON DOOR AUDIT DRAINED s2290 at `abf6b7464` — and the reconciliation the retraction ordered has an answer neither side expected: THE AUDIT'S VERDICT SURVIVES, ON THE RETRACTION'S OWN EVIDENCE.** Gated on the MERGED tree in detached `.gate-s2290` (§3.0b): tsc **rc=0**, `npm run build` **green 1.54 s** with the asset-diet ceiling respected. 10 paths (9 artifacts + the lane's own row), **RUN SURFACE 0**, firewall HELD exactly — so F-1460-1's `src/sim`|`src/systems`|`src/entities` trigger does not fire and the ~530 s battery was not re-run; this slice touches no code at all. 🔬 **The runner's headline was RE-DERIVED, not inherited (Mistake #4): both rows of its own `verification.md` reproduce EXACTLY on the merged tree** — `attempt-4-tape` → `fnv1a32:79cbfb15` and `h11-forward-rig-tape` → `fnv1a32:00d2c4f7`, both `secured:false waves:20 timeAlive:538.467`. Its arithmetic checks too (49,025 ÷ 53,346.893 = 8.10% burned = 12.34× short; the knife-edge `hpScale 240 → 19.44` is exactly that fraction applied to the current dial). 🕳️ **F-2290-1 (OPEN, non-blocking, OWNER-RELEVANT) — THE COUNTY'S ONLY CLAIMED AGENT BARON SECURE RETAINS NO TAPE.** The RETRACTION row above ordered this drain to reconcile against `6b1fcdce0`, and it does: that commit is REAL, it POSTDATES AP-16 (`git merge-base --is-ancestor 8465f6b33 6b1fcdce0` → yes), and it claims `secured:true waves:22 eventLogHash:fnv1a32:f5365f4c runsSoFar:6`. **But it landed exactly TWO files — `codex-sol-r1-outcome.json` and `codex-sol-r1-player.mjs` — and the tape its own outcome names, `run-6-tape.json`, is in NO commit: `git ls-files` matches it nowhere.** The only tracked occurrences of `f5365f4c` are the outcome's own self-report and a BACKLOG row citing it. ⚖️ **Stated honestly and NOT inflated — this is not an accusation that the secure was faked**; the player, outcome and campaign are mutually consistent and the run almost certainly happened as described. What is missing is the artifact that would let the county DEMONSTRATE it, which is a lesser claim than fraud but is exactly the claim `e1-baron`'s admission rests on. **So the audit's word `retained` was load-bearing and the retraction stepped past it: the verdict is STRENGTHENED, not corrected.** 🎯 **F-2290-2 (OPEN, non-blocking, PRICED, fire-authorable) — THE OWNER FORK IS PRICED AGAINST A STRATEGY NOBODY TRIED.** The audit recommends **(b) ACCEPTED-ELITE** because *"eleven distinct current-door hypotheses remain 12.34× short"* — sound about the eleven, silent about the twelfth, which is the only one that has ever worked. `bench/gauntlet/heat3/codex-sol-r1-player.mjs` **IS retained**: 195 lines, a full public-door plan (3 sluices, 4 turrets, 6 beacons, 3 palisades, 2 stockpiles, tiered upgrades, a scored `pickUpgrade`). **Unlike a tape, a player is a STRATEGY rather than a fixed input stream — and this morning's own `gauntlet-heat5b-reearn` drain (`77c85566a`, four hours earlier) established which of the two survives an engine patch: structural knowledge survives, tick-coupled timing does not.** The Aug-13 stream is engine-skewed and worthless; the Aug-13 STRATEGY is not, and it has never been re-ridden. ⚠️ **One caveat rides with it, UNMEASURED and named rather than hidden:** that plan builds **palisades**, and the corrected-by-the-ledger row argues the pre-law door offered agents an e1 palisade humans never had — the finding that birthed AP-16. The run postdates AP-16 by three days so the palisade was presumably in the manifest-derived buildable set it was gated against, but *presumably* is not *measured*, and if it was not, the strategy is unavailable and the fork's pricing stands unchanged. ➡️ **One cheap well-posed measurement resolves both questions in a single run — re-ride `codex-sol-r1-player.mjs` at the current engine and door, first bench seed — and it should precede the owner's ruling. Do NOT flip the admission on it either way; that is the owner's fork, and this only prices it.** 🔎 **F-2290-3 (OPEN, non-blocking) — THREE INDEPENDENT SWEEPS MISSED THE SAME RECORD FOR THE SAME REASON:** heat-5's study, attended's `find -name *baron*`, and this audit all failed to find `6b1fcdce0` because the campaign files carry **no contract name**, leaving the evidence discoverable only by reading commit subjects. The cure is an index entry, which the retraction already proposed as its consequence ④. 🔺 **OWNER FORK (unchanged by this drain, RE-PRICED by it):** (a) HP-only knife-edge `hpScale 240 → 19.44`, a 91.9% boss cut; (b) **ACCEPTED-ELITE** per the e9 precedent, honest exemption, non-debt; (c) standing bounty while exempt. The runner recommends **(b)** and this drain does not dispute it — it asks only that **F-2290-2's single re-ride be measured first**, because the recommendation's own reasoning is a count of failed hypotheses and the count is missing the one that succeeded. Review: `reviews/baron-door-audit.md`.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:707:✅ **gauntlet-heat3c-shim-streaming DRAINED + MERGED s2275 at `2e75540c1`** — the localhost Codex shim answers `stream:true` with buffered OpenAI-shape SSE (role · content/tool-call · finish+usage · `[DONE]`), and client abort now propagates an `AbortSignal` to the `codex exec` child. **This is the one cure four riders wait on:** heat-3b put Prime Agent 0.8.0, OMP 18.0.4, Hermes 0.20.0 and OpenClaw 2026.7.1-2 against the shim and ALL FOUR DNF'd on the same wall, `400 Streaming is not supported`. Gated on the MERGED tree in detached `gate-s2275/` (§3.0b): tsc **rc=0** 5.6 s · `npm run build` **rc=0** 17.3 s, asset-diet ceiling respected · shim suite **4 pass / 0 fail / 3 live arms skipped LOUDLY** on absent auth. 🎯 **THE GATE THAT MATTERS IS A FREE BEFORE/AFTER CONTROL, AND IT ASSERTS ITS OWN VALIDITY (F-2215-1):** with a fake `completeFn` (**zero Codex spend**) the merged tree returns **HTTP 200 `text/event-stream`, 4 SSE data lines, `[DONE]`** — while the SAME probe repointed at `main` pre-merge still returns **the exact `400 Streaming is not supported`**. So ARM A's green is a cure, not a probe that failed to run. Evidence: `artifacts/gauntlet-heat3c-20260824/wall-probe-before-after.md`. ⚖️ **Live arms deliberately NOT re-run:** merged-tree blobs for `serve.mjs`/`serve.test.mjs`/`codex-shim.md`/`package.json` are **BYTE-IDENTICAL** to the lane tree the runner gated, so its live measurement (**3 chunks, 16,749 tokens, 11.903 s vs 10.515 s non-streaming, zero orphans on abort**) transfers as a FACT — and re-spending ~16.7k of the owner's allowance would have pre-empted **F-2272-1, his own open desk question about exactly that cost**, while `lane-c` was concurrently BUSY on heat5 against the same subscription. All 4 files LANE-TOUCHED, zero BOTH-MOVED. Review: `reviews/gauntlet-heat3c-shim-streaming.md`. ➡️ **heat4 is UNBLOCKED on a CHANGED premise (§7.5)** — its STOP reason ("live `main` probe returned HTTP 400") is now measurably false.
