tasks/BACKLOG.md:2371:🟢 **F-1382-1 (s1382, MEASURED + CURED SAME FIRE — ❌ **F-1381-1 IS REFUTED**: THE E1 RELEASE DOOR WAS READING ROLLDOWN'S CONTENT HASH AS AN ERA TAG, AND IT HAD BEEN SHUT ON **CLEAN MAIN**, NOT BY ANY SLICE).** s1381 held lane-d `authored-bundle-validation` as BLOCKING on *"an E4 sprite chunk in the E1-only bundle"* — `char-bandit-base-sheet-walk8-r2c6-e4-RHTJh-diet-a9d5c9a0.js`. **There is no E4 asset.** That file is the **E1** frame `char-bandit-base-sheet-walk8-r2c6` carrying the content hash **`e4-RHTJh`**; its entire body is a `new URL(...)` wrapper pointing at `…-r2c6-Djmulw-f-diet-….png`, with **no `e4` anywhere**, and **no `-e4` bandit asset exists in the repo**. Dist basenames are `<module>-<hash>-diet-<fingerprint>` (`vite.config.ts:51-53`) and rolldown's `[hash]` is **base64url, which includes `-`**: **187 of 1869 hashes (10%) contained a hyphen**, so `assert-release-build.mjs`'s unanchored era regex, matched against the **whole basename**, fired on hash text. The match sits at index 33 — exactly the `…-r2c6` **/** `e4-RHTJh` boundary. ✓ **ATTRIBUTION REVERSED BY THE ONE ARM s1381 GOT WRONG: the CONTROL.** s1381 recorded *"clean main → GREEN"*; re-run on clean main `009251c7` it is **RED, identical error, identical hash**. Main's `src/` had not moved between the two runs. ✅ **MECHANISM PROVED BY MANUFACTURING IT, NOT ARGUED:** appending **one comment** to `scripts/asset-diet.mjs` — which changes the fingerprint token and **nothing about which assets are emitted** — flipped the gate **GREEN**. ⚠️ **And the green was itself controlled, because a gate that stops red-ing may simply have gone blind:** the rebuilt bundle held the **same 1869 files** with the **same sprite still emitted**, only the hash changed `e4-RHTJh` → `D2vmZunU`. A byte-identical asset set, opposite verdicts. 🔧 **CURED at `scripts/assert-release-build.mjs:54`** — era patterns now match the **module name only**, with the tail anchored `$` so a genuine era suffix survives hash-stripping. **Both directions proved:** clean main + fix builds **rc=0** (1874 files, 262-stem denominator, non-vacuous), and planted real era assets (`icons-e2-r0c3`, `char-tinkerer-e4`) **still fail**. 🔒 **Guarded by three cases in `scripts/assert-release-build.test.mjs`, and the pair is the point — dropping the false positive must not cost the real catch. Verified to RED at the pre-fix guard: exactly one of the three (the hash false positive) fails, while both positive controls stay green.** `test:node-guards` **rc=0**. 🚨 **BLAST RADIUS: `build:release` is the webServer for `playwright.release.config.ts`, so while this was red the release suite could not START AT ALL** — which is what **F-1381-2** saw from the other side. The fingerprint derives from `scripts/asset-diet.mjs`, last changed **2026-07-30 `5e129079`** (**INFERRED window — not bisected**). ⓘ **Why s1381's control came back green is UNVERIFIED and I will not guess it**; s1381 confessed a `node_modules`-symlink instrument failure in the same fire, so a control mismeasured in the opposite direction is the likely cause — a hypothesis, not a finding. 💡 **The class: an unanchored pattern matched against a generated filename is matching a namespace it does not own. Audited the siblings — `leakedAssets` and `laterEraAssets` are stem-anchored at `^` and NOT exposed, `laterEpoch` matches file contents for a literal a hash cannot mint — so the exposure was genuinely one check, not a family (F-1382-2, recorded so nobody re-derives it).** ➡️ **The through-line: s1380 said a control that cannot fail is not evidence. s1382 says the inverse and it is worse — a control that CAN fail, and did, can still be RECORDED WRONG, and everything built on it inherits the error. Three arms agreed with each other and all three were measuring the same pre-existing red. When every arm agrees, re-run the CONTROL, because that is the arm whose failure is invisible.** Full evidence: `reviews/release-door-hash-false-positive.md`.
tasks/BACKLOG.md:2597:🟡 **F-1307-2 (s1307, MEASURED — `logs/suite-red-inventory.md` LINE COORDINATES ROT WHENEVER A SPEC IS EDITED ABOVE A CITED LINE).** This drain shifted lines in 4 cited specs, rotting **18 citations**; all 18 repaired in the drain commit, **each verified by unique content match rather than by applying the net delta — which would have been wrong.** `asset-diet:101→:102` and `release-build:160→:161`/`:199→:200` moved **+1** (they sit above the deleted block but below the added import) while `cw-02-escort:134→:128` and `agent-view:283→:268` moved down 6 and 15. ⚠️ **Three were deliberately left alone and are NOT from this merge:** `release-build:107` and `:165` are generic brace lines with no unique content match, and **`release-build:393` already exceeded that file's 349 lines at HEAD** — pre-existing rot. ⓘ Severity is low **because the fingerprint's load-bearing columns are file + test name + project + error text**, and the line is supplementary — this very drain matched `cw-02-escort` on those three despite the stale line. Recorded so the class is known; not worth a guard yet.
